# AoC 2024 day 11: how many stones after blinking 25 and then 75 times.
#
# The stones never interact, so the answer is a sum over each starting stone
# independently — and the same (stone, blinks) question comes up over and over,
# which is exactly what `remember` is for. Without it this is 2^75 work.
digits n is pick (gt 9 n) (add 1 (digits (div n 10))) 1

pow10 0 is 1
pow10 k is mul 10 (pow10 (sub k 1))

remember stones s 0 is 1
stones 0 n is stones 1 (sub n 1)
stones s n is
  weave d is digits s
  weave half is pow10 (div d 2)
  pick (even d)
    (add (stones (div s half) (sub n 1)) (stones (mod s half) (sub n 1)))
    (stones (mul s 2024) (sub n 1))

start is Source | earths

[start | bend (s : stones s 25) | sum, start | bend (s : stones s 75) | sum]
  | bend air
  | join "\n"
